# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/prefix-tiers development window (the preconverted GDN checkpoints and the host KV tier; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/prefix-tiers and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are
# resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-prefix-tiers-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/prefix-tiers head (sed -i 's/tp4-prefix-tiers-1/<tag>/' *.env); every later job serves that one
# image. A commit of a file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# Q1 (STOP, the first card job of the tier): QUALIFY version 2 of the qwen_kv_read extension on the SERVED (1, 4) mesh (scripts/ci/tp4_kv_read_probe.py -> optimisation/ttnn-op/kv_region_read/kv_region_read_card.py run() and
# run_raw()): the region read against the whole-cache read as before, AND the raw block ops the host tier is built on: ttnn.qwen_read_blocks_raw reads the packed bytes of named blocks (every chip's page range), qwen_write_blocks_raw
# writes them into a second cache, the second cache read back byte for byte and unpacked equal, no program-cache growth, at 32/256/1024/4096 blocks (one 254k session is about 4,000 blocks), with the read and write rates
# in GB/s. READ: 'KV_READ_PROBE verdict=PASS', 'KV_READ_PROBE extension source: baked', and 'KV_READ_PROBE raw=ok' with its rate lines ('KV_READ_PROBE raw rate blocks=... read_gbps= write_gbps='): the rates are the
# device side of the tier's cost per 128k (about 2,000 blocks) and 254k (about 4,000), the numbers docs/prefix-store-hygiene.md plans with. raw=absent means the image bakes version 1 (the pin was not moved: B0's
# precondition); raw=FAIL (or any 'KV_READ_PROBE problem:' line) or verdict FAIL/NOT-MEASURED means the raw ops are NOT QUALIFIED: every later job of this pack is skipped. The probe opens the mesh once and closes it; a failed run needs a reset before the next hardware job.
# The box is the probe's own timeout (the workflow bounds the docker run by it): 30 minutes under the fabric step's 45. Duration (estimate): 12 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset fabric
C2_FABRIC_PROBE=kvread
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-prefix-tiers-1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=30
